  "notes": "West leads the ♠K against 2♥. West cashes the 2 top spades and gives East a spade ruff. East plays a trump, won in dummy. South still has certain losers in both diamonds and clubs. South should try to ruff his second club loser in the dummy.\n\nIf South cashes the ♣A and surrenders a club trick, the defense will play another heart. South will have no quick way back to his hand to ruff his remaining club loser. The defenders may be in a position to gain the lead in diamonds and lead a third round of trump, removing all of North's hearts.\n\nSouth does better by ducking the first round of clubs. He wins the heart return and crosses to his hand with the ♣A. South ruffs his club loser and concedes a diamond trick.",
